phase P2
title Runtime ownership

tasks
    T201
        title        Establish no-persistence Runtime readiness
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T103,
                     @task.Rewrite.T104,
                     @task.Rewrite.T105, 
                     @task.Rewrite.T107,
                     @task.Rewrite.T108
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O3,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V3,
                     @plan.Persistence.O1,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        description
            Implement the base shared Runtime bootstrap for a closed App and exact Implementation 
            with persistence disabled. Keep construct/discovery inert and make ready() the single 
            readiness boundary. This is an incremental readiness result; durable selection, 
            detached restore, and full persistence-aware outcome closure remain in P4.
        acceptance
            Controlled positive/failure vectors prove construction performs no 
            acquisition/actor/work/evidence; one readiness attempt shares success/failure across 
            waiters; interruption of one waiter does not cancel another; disposal racing late 
            readiness cannot reopen admission; rollback finalizes acquired owners in reverse order 
            and caches terminal failure truth. Run `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/readiness.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/assembly.test.ts` and `nub run 
            --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`; all pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/**` and readiness fixtures. Evidence: 
            readiness/assembly tests and type fixtures. This Task derives from App.O3/V3 but does 
            not satisfy persistence-aware clauses; P4 boot/restore Tasks own those remaining 
            clauses.

    T202
        title        Admit actors through one shared lease
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T201]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O4,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V4,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O4]
        description
            Implement exact ActorRef admission, one shared actor/lease per Runtime identity, 
            compatible context bindings, and clean unpublished retry. Keep refs inert and 
            non-authoritative; handles and refs cannot dispose actors.
        acceptance
            Positive/failure/race vectors prove concurrent ensures join one admission and first 
            accepted input initializes once; compatible fixed bindings share admission; conflicting 
            bindings and missing/foreign/tombstoned refs reject unchanged before work. An 
            unpublished failure rolls back once and permits a later clean attempt; post-visibility 
            failure uses terminal disposal. `get` creates or leases nothing; `create` returns 
            distinct opaque refs. Run `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/actor-admission.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/actor-lease-owner.test.ts` and `nub 
            run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`; all pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/actor/**` and focused admission fixtures. 
            Evidence: admission/lease tests and compile fixtures.

    T203
        title        Enforce actor lifecycle and terminal cleanup
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T201, @T202]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O5,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V5,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O5]
        description
            Implement prepared/active/suspended/disposed transitions, ownership boundaries, 
            dependent-provider protection, asynchronous idempotent disposal, and reverse-dependency 
            Runtime cleanup. Preserve queued finite work and finalizer truth across suspension and 
            termination.
        acceptance
            Controlled lifecycle/race/failure vectors prove prepared actors buffer only bounded 
            commands, active actors admit, suspended actors reject without buffering and preserve 
            continuity, and disposed actors remain terminal. Only leases or Runtime shutdown 
            dispose; dependent providers reject before cleanup begins and identify blocked 
            refs/keys. Suspension drains or retires queued work exactly once, waits for finalizers, 
            preserves identity/deadlines, and resume does not replay. Cleanup defects prevent false 
            resume/success; repeated disposal joins the same cached result without rerunning 
            finalizers. Run `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/lifecycle.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/actor-engine-owner.test.ts` and `nub 
            run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`; all pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/actor/**` and lifecycle fixtures. 
            Evidence: lifecycle/engine tests.

    T204
        title        Bind fixed context from one admitted provider cut
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T102, @T202, @T203]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O6,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V6,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        description
            Implement exact typed provider selection, binding identity, and silent baseline 
            installation for admitted actor refs. Reject incomplete, foreign, closing, disposed, or 
            cyclic provider graphs before effects. Causal multi-provider waves are a separate Task.
        acceptance
            Positive and negative type/runtime vectors prove one fixed binding per consumer 
            lifetime from an atomic exact provider snapshot, silent baseline installation, and 
            deterministic provider/consumer topology. Missing, ambiguous, foreign, incompatible, 
            closing, disposed, tombstoned, unresolvable, or cyclic providers reject before effects 
            and without partial bindings. Opaque local actor identity is accepted only when 
            admitted authority is verifiable. Run `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/context-lineage-owner.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/context.test.ts` and `nub run 
            --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`; all pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/context/**`, actor admission integration, 
            and focused context fixtures. Evidence: context tests and type fixtures.

    T205
        title        Implement causal context waves after selector policy is settled
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T204, @T206]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O6,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.Q1,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V6,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O6]
        description
            Implement provider/consumer context waves, retained complete truth, equal settlement, 
            debt, and retry behavior only after T206 resolves the selector-defect policy. Keep 
            actor admission/baseline work independently usable while this question-bound slice is 
            draft.
        acceptance
            Once the owning Question is explicitly resolved, controlled chain/diamond vectors prove 
            consumers never publish mixed old/new provider truth, equal-valued settlement clears 
            debt without a value-change event, queued wakes use latest complete truth, and blocked 
            heads preserve FIFO. The approved selector-defect behavior is tested for 
            provider/sibling commit, retained context, issue/event publication, and retry trigger. 
            Suspended debt rejects capture until explicit recovery. Run focused production 
            context-wave tests and `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`; both pass. 
            Write scope: `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/context/**` and context-wave 
            fixtures. Evidence: context-wave/debt tests. Do not implement a candidate answer before 
            T206 is approved.

    T206
        title        Resolve selector-defect isolation and retry policy
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.Q1,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V6,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O4
                     ]
        description
            Obtain the explicit owner decision for ApplicationsAndActors.Q1 about provider/sibling 
            commit, retained consumer context, issue-only publication, and retry trigger. Keep this 
            decision local to the affected causal-wave slice; it must not block unrelated 
            admission, actor-only turns, or operation kernels.
        acceptance
            Record the owner-approved answer to the exact Q1 alternatives and its effect on V6 
            before T205 implementation begins. No runtime behavior is chosen or inferred by this 
            Task. This decision task remains draft until the required Plan decision is approved.

    T207
        title        Bound mailbox admission and preserve reentrant FIFO
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T102, @T202, @T203]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O7,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V7,
                     @plan.Statecharts.O3,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        description
            Implement synchronous typed send admission with documented finite prepared/active 
            capacity, no-mutation overload rejection, and reentrant FIFO sequencing. The proof 
            covers mailbox decisions only and does not depend on the selector-defect Question in 
            T206.
        acceptance
            Positive/failure vectors prove exact EventOf<Machine> admission, documented finite 
            prepared/active limits (prepared supports at least 64 commands), and FIFO for reentrant 
            accepted sends. At capacity reject the whole new admission synchronously with 
            AdmissionOverloaded before event occurrence, state/store mutation, evidence, or work; 
            suspended/disposed actors reject without buffering. Run `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/actor-admission.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/turns.test.ts` and `nub run --filter 
            flow-state-rewrite check:types`; all pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/actor/actor-mailbox.ts`, actor 
            admission/engine integration, and focused mailbox fixtures. Evidence: mailbox/admission 
            tests and type fixtures.

    T208
        title        Commit actor macrosteps before asynchronous work
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T105, @task.Rewrite.T106, @T207]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Statecharts.O3,
                     @plan.Statecharts.V3,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O7,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V7,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O2,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.V2,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        description
            Implement actor-only event decisions: ordered guard/update/action evaluation against 
            the pre-turn snapshot, redirect stabilization, whole-batch validation, issue-only 
            failure truth, no-op behavior, and committed publication before starting work. 
            Store/operation/evidence integration remains with P3 T313.
        acceptance
            Positive, decline, no-op, and failure vectors prove updateMemory precedes actions while 
            both see the same pre-turn snapshot; actions cannot see candidate memory; redirects see 
            candidate state/memory only; complete batches validate before mutation; a valid prefix 
            of an invalid batch leaves no partial commit or work. No handler/all-decline creates no 
            revision/evidence/work. Guard/action/redirect/key defects preserve prior domain truth 
            and publish one issue-only cut without retry. A successful actor-only turn publishes 
            one committed cut before any user Effect/work. Run `nubx vp test 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/turn-plan-owner.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/turns.test.ts` and `nub run --filter 
            flow-state-rewrite check:types`; all pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/actor/**`, `turn-plan.ts`, and focused 
            turn fixtures. Evidence: turn-plan/turn tests. Operation/store/evidence atomicity is 
            explicitly deferred to T313.

    T209
        title        Own continuing declarations and timer lifetimes
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T102, @task.Rewrite.T106, @T203, @T208]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Statecharts.O4,
                     @plan.Statecharts.V4,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O5,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V5,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Statecharts.O4]
        description
            Implement actor-owned state activities, independent onMemory declaration slots, 
            selector equality, timer scheduling/fencing, deadline ordering, and 
            cancellation/reentry cleanup. Keep operation execution and stream identity integration 
            with P3 owners.
        acceptance
            Positive/failure/race vectors prove one private slot per state/onMemory declaration, 
            equal identity retains original input/generation, changed identity releases once before 
            replacement, false/null releases only its slot, and parent activities survive 
            child-only changes. Verify scalar Object.is and fixed-key record equality, exactly-once 
            cleanup, absolute deadline preservation, generation-fenced stale timer rejection, 
            equal-deadline ordering, and no replay on resume. Invalid delay/action input leaves 
            state unchanged. Run focused actor activity/timer tests and `nub run --filter 
            flow-state-rewrite check:types`; both pass. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/actor/actor-activities.ts`, 
            `actor-timer-work.ts`, and focused fixtures. Evidence: activity/timer tests. 
            Stream/resource adapter start, release and cancellation proofs remain with P3.

    T210
        title        Publish actor snapshots/evidence and close the settled P2 gate
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T107,
                     @T201,
                     @T202,
                     @T203,
                     @T204,
                     @T207,
                     @T208,
                     @T209
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O7,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.V7,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V3,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        description
            Implement immutable current actor snapshots, prepared replay, slow-reader latest-value 
            behavior, and actor-only evidence acceptance/acknowledgment ordering. Close settled P2 
            Runtime-ownership work after T201–T204 and T207–T209 pass. The actor-only gate 
            explicitly leaves selector-defect behavior under T206/T205 and canonical 
            store/operation integration to P3/P4.
        acceptance
            Positive/failure vectors prove a reader always receives a complete immutable current 
            actor snapshot, may skip obsolete snapshots, and cannot mutate past state. Prepared 
            subscription replays the current prepared snapshot; suspended/disposed subscription 
            replays final state then completes. Actor acknowledgment follows publication and 
            private evidence acceptance but does not wait for user Effects or sinks. Evidence 
            bounds/exhaustion reject before mutation or reserve terminal cleanup capacity. Run 
            `nubx vp test packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/actor-evidence.test.ts 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/test/evidence-record-owner.test.ts` and 
            `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types`; both pass. Confirm the settled P2 
            owner checks pass. This gate does not wait on T205/T206 or claim full actor/store 
            publication. Write scope: 
            `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime-next/actor/actor-snapshot.ts`, 
            `actor-evidence.ts`, `evidence-record.ts`, `evidence-journal.ts`, 
            `evidence-acceptance.ts`, `evidence-sequencer.ts`, and actor evidence fixtures. P4 T408 
            alone owns `evidence-sink.ts` and sink ownership tests. Evidence: actor 
            snapshot/evidence tests. Store fanout and complete actor/store/lifecycle cuts remain 
            with P3 T313 and P4 T415.
